.TH NM 1 "September 19, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
nm \- print object-file symbols
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nm
.RB [ \-ug ]
.I file ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Nm
prints the symbol table from the output file of an assembler run.
The output is sorted alphabetically.
On maux the files must be Merlin-format REL objects.
Each line has an address, type letter and name.
.TP
.B X
An exported definition (ENT). The address is module-relative.
.TP
.B U
An external reference (EXT), undefined in this module.
.TP
.B \-u
Print only undefined symbols.
.TP
.B \-g
Print only exported definitions.
.PP
The two selections intersect: -ug prints no symbols.
More than one operand produces a file-name header for each table.
Unlike historical nm, there is no default a.out operand.
.SH FILES
/usr/man/NM  this page
.SH "SEE ALSO"
nas(1), as(1), ld(1), licenses(1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Exit status is 0 on success, 1 for file/format failures, 2 for usage errors.
.SH BUGS
Ordinary private assembler labels are not present in the REL dictionary and cannot be displayed. There is no T/D/B distinction.
